    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1950957963516244062",
      "url": "https://x.com/muugeeverse/status/1950957963516244062",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/muugeeverse/status/1950957963516244062",
      "text": "This is why local-first compute isn’t optional anymore.\n\nCentralized cloud often routes traffic across countries or continents, like Manila to Virginia adding 150–300ms of delay. For real-time apps, that’s a dealbreaker.\n\n@theblessnetwork changes that.\nWith Extension Nodes live and Desktop Nodes coming soon, compute happens near you, on everyday devices.\nAs more nodes come online, we’re already seeing latency drop to 20–30ms in early zones.\n\nThe result? Faster apps, smoother voice, responsive AI.\nThis is the internet that's fast and efficient.",
