      "quoted_tweet": {
        "type": "tweet",
        "id": "1950916750054474009",
        "url": "https://x.com/muugeeverse/status/1950916750054474009",
        "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/muugeeverse/status/1950916750054474009",
        "text": "We’ve all been there, joining a community space with an app, you connect, but there’s that awkward few seconds of silence. You’re wondering if it’s broken… then suddenly voices come through, and you thought your Internet connection is the problem.\n\nThat lag? It’s usually because the server you’re hitting is halfway across the world.\n\nCentralized cloud can introduce 100–300ms+ latency, especially across continents.\n\n@theblessnetwork solves that by running compute through Extension node and soon Desktop node closer to you, latency drops to <30ms in many cases and Bless can drop it down to 20ms as it scale.\n\nCloser compute = smoother experience.\nIt’s not just faster, it feels instant.\nKeep running your node folks, $BLESS is coming.",
